# Files that must never be committed to this repository.

# --- 06-temp/ is scratch space -------------------------------------------------
# The folder convention says "always safe to delete", which only holds if its
# contents stay out of git. Without this rule a scratch file lands in a commit
# the first time anyone runs `git add -A`; a committed dev script once shipped
# a live test password to this public repo.
06-temp/*
!06-temp/.gitkeep
!06-temp/README.md

# --- python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces: the canonical env files live in 05-config/, but keep .env
# out of git anywhere it appears.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- local agent/tooling state ------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.hermes/

# Mutation-testing scratch copies. A stray `scripts/*.py.bak` in a commit is how
# an old version of a security-relevant tool ends up back in the tree.
*.bak
